  "notes": "USAGE:\nPrimarily used for running races (marathons, relays) and motorsport (F1, car rallies). The focus is on completing the course, not on placement. For many amateur runners, {完走|かんそう} itself is the goal.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- マラソンを{完走|かんそう}する (to finish a marathon)\n- {完走|かんそう}{証|しょう} (completion certificate)\n- {完走|かんそう}タイム (finishing time)\n- {完走|かんそう}{率|りつ} (completion rate)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ゴール: goal, finish line — the physical endpoint\n- {完|かん}{走|そう} vs {感想|かんそう} vs {乾燥|かんそう}: these are homophones — be careful with context",
